T[3755]=dict(
title="Morocco Cycling Tour: Atlas Mountains & Sahara Desert",
ov=["Eight days, six of them on the bike, from Marrakech over the High Atlas to the edge of the Sahara. You ride past Ait Ben Haddou, down through the palm groves of the Draa Valley, across dry lakes and out to the Chegaga dunes, where you spend a night under a sky full of stars.",
    "The riding is mostly on quiet back roads and desert tracks, so it suits a mountain bike, a gravel bike or an e-bike. A 4x4 support vehicle stays with the group every day, so you can take a break in the car whenever you need one."],
facts=[("Tour name","Biking the Atlas Mountains and the Chegaga Dunes"),("Duration","8 days, 6 days of cycling"),("Grade","Moderate"),("Best time to visit","March to December"),("Bike","Mountain bike, gravel bike or e-bike"),("Group size","2 to 16 riders"),("Recommended age","16 to 65"),("Start / finish","Marrakech"),("Accommodation","Hotels, a desert camp and a guesthouse (gîte)")],
inc=["Meals: 7 breakfasts, 6 lunches and 6 dinners, plus mineral water","All meals during the tour except dinner on day 7","Accommodation: 6 nights in hotels and 1 night in a desert camp","Rooms are twin share; a single room is available for a supplement of 450 EUR","Transport by comfortable van or Toyota Land Cruiser (4x4), including airport transfers on day 1 and day 8","A 4x4 support vehicle with the riders every day","6 days of guided cycling","Visit of Jemaa el-Fna square and the old medina of Marrakech","Visit of Ait Ben Haddou, a UNESCO World Heritage Site","Riding through the Draa Valley and the Chegaga desert"],
exc=["Flights and visas","Meals not listed in the itinerary","Tips","Alcoholic drinks","Laundry and souvenirs","Personal travel insurance","Bike hire (mountain bike, gravel bike or e-bike). You can bring your own bike or rent one from us."],
hl=["Explore the old medina of Marrakech","Cross the Atlas Mountains and ride into the Sahara","Cycle to Ait Ben Haddou, a UNESCO World Heritage Site","Six full days of riding in southern Morocco","Sleep under the stars in the Chegaga dunes","Ride through the palm groves of the Draa oasis"],
it={1:("Arrival in Marrakech","We meet you at Marrakech Menara Airport and drive you to your hotel, 15 minutes away. In the evening your guide runs through the tour with the group. If you have time, wander through the old town, Bahia Palace and Jemaa el-Fna square."),
2:("Marrakech to Ouarzazate","We leave the city and climb into the Atlas over the Tizi n'Tichka pass (2,260 m). The land turns dry and red as we reach Ait Ben Haddou, the old ksar you may know from Lawrence of Arabia and Gladiator. After lunch we get on the bikes and ride through small villages to Ouarzazate, the 'city of cinema'."),
3:("Ouarzazate and the Draa Valley","A one-hour drive takes us to Tizi n'Tinifift (1,800 m), with a view over the volcanic Jebel Saghro and the Draa Valley, Morocco's longest valley at about 1,200 km. From there it's mostly downhill to the Tizgui waterfall and the first oasis. We ride through Berber villages and stop for mint tea with a local family."),
4:("Mezguita to Zagora","Today we follow the Draa oasis, where desert sand meets tall green palms. The river road gives some of the best views in southern Morocco. After 55 km on the bike, the 4x4 takes us the last 50 km to Zagora, the traditional gateway to the Sahara."),
5:("Zagora to Erg Lihoudi","Desert day. A short 4x4 drive takes us to Tamegroute and its Koranic library, which dates back to the 11th century. From there we ride into the Sahara on a varied route over dry lakes and past small green oases, all the way to our camp in the dunes of Erg Lihoudi. Dinner and the night are under the stars."),
6:("Erg Lihoudi to the Chegaga dunes and Foum Zguid","We drive 50 km across the dunes to Lake Iriqi, a dry salt lake where nomads still pass with their camels. Then we ride along the flat lakebed toward Foum Zguid, where we sleep in a kasbah hotel."),
7:("Foum Zguid to Taznakht and Marrakech","The last ride is an easy 30 km through quiet oases and Berber villages. From Taznakht we drive back to Marrakech for the night."),
8:("Departure","Transfer to Menara Airport for your flight. Check-out is at 11:30. We hope to ride with you again – ma'a salama!")})
T[3723]=dict(
title="Caravan Road Gravel Bike Tour",
ov=["This 8-day gravel bike tour starts and ends in Marrakech. You ride along the Atlas range and over the volcanic Jebel Saghro, following the old caravan road through quiet gorges, kasbahs and valleys until you reach the Draa Valley, Morocco's longest oasis.",
    "It's a proper back-country route: five days of riding on dirt roads, with nights in kasbah hotels and family-run guesthouses."],
facts=[("Tour name","Caravan Road by Gravel Bike"),("Duration","8 days, 5 days of cycling"),("Grade","Moderate"),("Best time to visit","March to November"),("Bike","Gravel bike or mountain bike"),("Group size","Up to 16 riders"),("Recommended age","16 to 65"),("Start / finish","Marrakech"),("Accommodation","Hotels and guesthouses (gîtes)")],
inc=["Meals: 7 breakfasts, 6 lunches and 5 dinners, plus mineral water (all meals during the tour except dinner on day 1 and day 7)","Accommodation: 7 nights (5 in hotels, 2 in guesthouses)","Transport by comfortable van or Toyota Land Cruiser (4x4), including airport transfers","5 days of guided cycling, plus visits to Jemaa el-Fna, Ouarzazate and the Draa Valley"],
exc=["Flights and visas","Meals not listed in the itinerary","Tips and alcoholic drinks","Personal travel insurance","Bike hire. You can bring your own bike or rent one from us."],
hl=["Explore the old medina of Marrakech","Five days of riding through the High Atlas and Anti-Atlas","A night in the Draa Valley, the longest oasis in Africa","Visit Ouarzazate and its film studios"],
it={1:("Welcome to Marrakech","We pick you up at Marrakech Menara Airport and drive you to the hotel. Later you meet your guide for a short briefing. With any time left, walk around the old town, Bahia Palace and Jemaa el-Fna square."),
2:("Marrakech to Skoura Oasis","We drive south over the High Atlas to the village of Ghassat, where the riding begins. The track runs over red earth and along the river to the Skoura oasis. It's an easy first day to find your rhythm. Night in a kasbah hotel."),
3:("Skoura Oasis to the Dades Gorges","A short drive takes us to Souk El Had. From there we ride across the Azaghar plateau, nomad country where some Berber families still live in caves. After lunch we continue through the Kati gorges and the Rose Valley to the Dades Gorges. Night in a guesthouse."),
4:("Dades Gorges and Jebel Saghro","We ride from the guesthouse toward the remote Berber villages of Jebel Saghro. A short climb to Boumalne Dades is followed by 15 flat kilometres. After tea with a local family, we cross the rocky Saghro massif to our guesthouse."),
5:("Jebel Saghro to the Draa Valley","The day starts with a 5 km climb to the high Saghro plateau and wide views back to the High Atlas. After 15 km of rolling terrain, we drop down the old caravan route into the Draa Valley. Night in a kasbah hotel."),
6:("Draa Valley and the Tizgui waterfall","An easy day, mostly flat or downhill, through the oasis and past old mud-brick villages. We stop for a picnic in the palm groves before reaching the Tizgui waterfall, then transfer to Ouarzazate for the night."),
7:("Ouarzazate to Marrakech via Ait Ben Haddou","After breakfast we follow the caravan road through a green oasis to Ait Ben Haddou, famous as a film location. After lunch there's time for a walk through the old kasbah village, then we drive back to Marrakech."),
8:("Departure","Transfer to Menara Airport for your flight. Check-out is at 11:30. We hope to see you on another gravel ride soon – ma'a salama!")})
T[3761]=dict(
title="Morocco Hike and Bike Tour: Happy Valley, Lake and Waterfall",
ov=["Can't choose between hiking and cycling? This 8-day tour gives you both. You spend two full days walking in the Ait Bouguemez, the 'Happy Valley', below M'Goun (4,071 m), the second-highest mountain in Morocco. Then you ride for three days through the M'Goun Geopark to Bin El Ouidane lake and the Ouzoud waterfalls.",
    "The walking is easy, the riding is moderate, and the 4x4 is always close by. It's a good choice for couples and groups with mixed fitness."],
facts=[("Tour name","Morocco Hike and Bike Tour"),("Duration","8 days: 2 days hiking and 3 days cycling"),("Grade","Easy to moderate"),("Best time to visit","March to November"),("Bike","Gravel bike, mountain bike or e-bike"),("Group size","2 to 16 people"),("Recommended age","16 to 65"),("Start / finish","Marrakech"),("Accommodation","Hotels, a camp and guesthouses (gîtes)")],
inc=["Meals: 7 breakfasts, 6 lunches and 6 dinners, plus mineral water","All meals during the tour except dinner on day 1 and day 7 in Marrakech","Accommodation: 3 nights in hotels, 3 nights in guesthouses and 1 night in a camp","Rooms are twin share; a single room is available for a supplement of 395 EUR","Transport by comfortable van or Toyota Land Cruiser (4x4), including airport transfers on day 1 and day 8","A 4x4 support vehicle with the riders every day","3 days of guided cycling and 2 days of guided hiking","Visit of Jemaa el-Fna square and the old medina of Marrakech","Visit of the Ouzoud waterfalls and Bin El Ouidane lake"],
exc=["Flights and visas","Meals not listed in the itinerary","Tips","Alcoholic drinks","Laundry and souvenirs","Personal travel insurance","Bike hire (mountain bike, gravel bike or e-bike). You can bring your own bike or rent one from us."],
hl=["Explore the old medina of Marrakech","Hike and bike in the Atlas Mountains","A night by Bin El Ouidane lake","See the Ouzoud waterfalls","Walk through the Happy Valley"],
it={1:("Arrival in Marrakech","We meet you at Marrakech Menara Airport and drive you to your hotel, 15 minutes away. Later you meet your guide for a briefing about the tour. If you have time, visit the old town, Bahia Palace and Jemaa el-Fna square."),
2:("Marrakech to the Ait Bouguemez Valley","A five-hour drive takes us into the mountains, with a stop at the natural bridge of Imi n'Ifri and lunch in the village of Ait Bouali. In the Happy Valley we meet the muleteers and walk for an hour to our guesthouse."),
3:("Tizi n'Ait Imi and the Sidi Moussa granary","A 4–5 hour walk takes us through the heart of the valley. We climb up to Sidi Moussa, an old hilltop granary where families kept their grain in small rooms. In the afternoon we walk up the valley from village to village to our guesthouse in Ait Imi."),
4:("Ait Imi to Zaouit Oulmzi","We walk through the village of Ibaqalliwn to see dinosaur footprints left in the rock millions of years ago. Then we continue to Adazen for a great view of the valley. After lunch we go down to Zaouit Oulmzi for the night."),
5:("Ait Bouguemez to Assamar","Breakfast on the terrace comes with a view of M'Goun (4,071 m). Then we get on the bikes. The first 8 km are easy, through potato fields and apple orchards. Then comes the hardest climb of the day, up to the Tizi n'Tirghist pass, with a big view of the Atlas range. After lunch a more technical stretch takes us up and down to our camp at Assamar."),
6:("Assamar to Bin El Ouidane lake","Today's ride winds up and down through a long, quiet thuya forest on good gravel. It's a demanding but very rewarding day. We finish at the lake with a glass of mint tea at our hotel."),
7:("Bin El Ouidane to Ouzoud and Marrakech","After a short transfer to Azilal, the last ride is mostly downhill through oak forests and olive groves, with a few short climbs. We reach the Ouzoud waterfalls in the early afternoon and have lunch with a view of the falls. Then we drive back to Marrakech, where the medina is at its liveliest in the evening."),
8:("Departure","Transfer to Menara Airport for your flight. Check-out is at 11:30. We hope to see you again soon – ma'a salama!")})
